1. Chosen Development Model
Agile is our chosen development technique because the project requires flexibility and continuous improvement. Since student needs and housing availability may change frequently, Agile allows iterative development, quick feedback, and regular updates. It also supports collaboration between developers and users, ensuring the app meets real student needs.
2. User Requirements
a. Stakeholders
Students: 
Looking for apartments or roommates. They want affordable, safe, and convenient housing.
Landlords:
Want to list properties, find reliable tenants, and manage listings
Administrator:
Responsible for building, maintaining, oversees the platform, ensuring safety, accuracy, and smooth operation.
b. User Stories
As a student, I want to create an account so that I can access housing listings.
As a student, I want to search for apartments by location so that I can find housing near my university.
As a student, I want to filter listings by price so that I can find affordable options.
As a student, I want to connect with roommates so that I can share rent costs.
As a student, I want to chat with other users so that I can discuss housing details.
As a landlord, I want to post apartment listings so that I can find tenants.
As a landlord, I want to edit or remove listings so that I can keep information updated.
As a student, I want to view detailed apartment information so that I can make informed decisions.
As a student, I want to save favorite listings so that I can review them later.
As a user, I want secure login so that my data is protected.


3. Functional Requirements



1. User Registration
The system should allow users to register and create an account.
Acceptance Criteria:
User enters name, email, and password
System validates all fields
Email must be unique
Account is created successfully
Confirmation message is shown

2. User Login
Description:
The system should allow users to log in.
Acceptance Criteria:
User enters valid email and password
System verifies credentials
User is redirected to dashboard
Error message is shown for invalid login

3. Profile Management
Description:
The system should allow users to update their profile.
Acceptance Criteria:
User edits profile information
System validates input
Changes are saved successfully
Updated information is displayed

4. Upload Profile Picture
Description:
The system should allow users to upload a profile picture.
Acceptance Criteria:
User selects image file
System uploads image
Image is displayed on profile
Error shown for invalid format

5. Filter Listings
Description:
The system should allow users to filter listings.
Acceptance Criteria:
User selects filters (price, location, type)
System updates results instantly
Only matching listings are shown

6. Create Listing
Description:
The system should allow landlords to create listings.
Acceptance Criteria:
Landlord enters all required fields
System validates input
Listing is saved successfully
Listing appears in search results

7. Delete Listing
Description:
The system should allow landlords to delete listings.
Acceptance Criteria:
Landlord selects delete option
System confirms action
Listing is removed
Listing no longer appears

8. Save Favorites
Description:
The system should allow users to save listings.
Acceptance Criteria:
User clicks save button
Listing is added to favorites
Favorites list updates
User can remove saved listings

9. View Favorites
Description:
The system should allow users to view saved listings.
Acceptance Criteria:
User opens favorites section
Saved listings are displayed
Listings are clickable

10. Send Messages (Chatbox)
Description:
The system should allow users to send messages.
Acceptance Criteria:
User opens chat
User types and sends message
Message is delivered instantly
Message appears for both users

11. Real-Time Chat
Description:
The system should support real-time communication.
Acceptance Criteria:
Messages appear instantly
No page refresh needed
Chat updates automatically

12. Chat History
Description:
The system should store previous messages.
Acceptance Criteria:
Messages are saved
User can scroll chat history
Messages are displayed in order

13. Message Notifications
Description:
The system should notify users of new messages.
Acceptance Criteria:
Notification appears for new message
Sender name is displayed
Notification disappears after viewing

14. Report Listings/Users
Description:
The system should allow users to report issues.
Acceptance Criteria:
User selects report option
User submits reason
Report is sent to admin
Confirmation message is shown

15. Admin Management
Description:
The system should allow admins to manage users and listings.
Acceptance Criteria:
Admin can view users
Admin can remove users/listings
Changes are applied immediately

16. Roommate Matching System
Description:
The system should match students based on preferences.
Acceptance Criteria:
User selects preferences (budget, habits, location)
System suggests compatible roommates
Matches are displayed clearly

17.Interactive Map Search
Description:
The system should display apartments on a map.
Acceptance Criteria:
Listings appear on map view
User can zoom and move map
Clicking a location shows listing details
Map updates based on filters

18. Budget Split Calculator
Description:
The system should help users calculate shared rent.
Acceptance Criteria:
User enters total rent and number of roommates
System calculates individual cost
Results are displayed instantly
Users can adjust values

19. Availability Calendar
Description:
The system should show apartment availability dates.
Acceptance Criteria:
Landlord sets availability dates
Calendar is visible to users
Users can view available periods
Booked dates are blocked

20.In-App Appointment Scheduling
Description:
The system should allow users to schedule visits.
Acceptance Criteria:
User selects date and time
Landlord receives request
Confirmation is sent
Appointment appears in schedule




4. Non-Functional Requirements



1. Student-Friendly Response Time
Description:
The system should provide fast responses tailored to student needs.
Acceptance Criteria:
Search results load in under 1.5 seconds
Chat messages deliver in under 0.8 seconds
Calendar updates appear instantly

2. Gamified Engagement
Description:
The system should encourage active participation via gamification (badges, rewards).
Acceptance Criteria:
Users receive badges for completing profiles, posting reviews, or reporting issues
Points are updated in real-time
Rewards are displayed on dashboard

3. Context-Aware Notifications
Description:
Notifications should adapt to user behavior and context.
Acceptance Criteria:
Only relevant alerts are shown (new matches, apartment availability, chat messages)
User can customize notification frequency
Notifications are delivered within 1 second of trigger

4. Visual Feedback
Description:
The system should provide clear visual feedback for user actions.
Acceptance Criteria:
Buttons change state on click
Loading indicators show progress
Users know immediately if actions succeeded or failed

5. Adaptive Mobile Experience
Description:
The system should optimize layout based on device and network quality.
Acceptance Criteria:
UI adjusts for small screens (<6 inches)
Low-bandwidth mode loads essential content first
No elements overlap or break

6. Real-Time Safety Alerts
Description:
The system should notify students of potentially risky listings or users.
Acceptance Criteria:
Unsafe behavior triggers alert
Alerts appear in app instantly
Admin receives automatic report

7. Social Proof Integration
Description:
The system should show reviews and ratings for listings and landlords.
Acceptance Criteria:
Ratings display immediately after submission
Users can filter listings by reviews
Reviews cannot be altered once posted

8. Multi-Profile Management
Description:
The system should allow users to manage multiple profiles (e.g., student & roommate seeker).
Acceptance Criteria:
Users can switch profiles without logging out
Each profile maintains separate data
Actions are correctly attributed to selected profile

9. Energy-Efficient Operation
Description:
The app should minimize battery and data usage.
Acceptance Criteria:
Background chat updates consume minimal battery
Images load progressively to save data
CPU usage remains under 30% during normal operations

10. AI-Powered Fraud Detection
Description:
The system should detect fake listings automatically.
Acceptance Criteria:
Suspicious listings are flagged
Admin receives automated alerts
Users are warned before contacting flagged listings

11. Privacy by Design
Description:
The system should protect sensitive student data automatically.
Acceptance Criteria:
Default privacy settings limit profile visibility
Users can control who sees personal information
Chat history is encrypted

12. Multi-Language Adaptation
Description:
The system should adapt content to multiple languages.
Acceptance Criteria:
Interface supports at least 3 languages
Translations are contextually accurate
User can switch language without reloading

13. AI-Based Search Ranking
Description:
The system should rank search results using AI based on relevance.
Acceptance Criteria:
Most relevant listings appear first
Rankings adjust dynamically to user behavior
Users can manually override rankings

14. Stress-Tested Load Handling
Description:
The system should handle student rush hours (start of semester).
Acceptance Criteria:
Supports 2,000+ concurrent users
Search and chat performance remains smooth
No crashes during peak hours

15. Offline Mode Preview
Description:
The system should allow users to view saved listings offline.
Acceptance Criteria:
Previously saved listings load without internet
Chat requires connection, but other features work offline
Offline data syncs automatically when online

16. Customizable Dashboard
Description:
The system should let users customize their home screen.
Acceptance Criteria:
Users can reorder modules (matches, listings, chat)
Changes are saved automatically
Dashboard updates dynamically

17. Continuous Improvement Feedback Loop
Description:
The system should collect anonymous feedback for improvement.
Acceptance Criteria:
Feedback form is available in app
User suggestions are collected automatically
Admin receives summarized reports weekly

18. Interactive Help System
Description:
The system should provide contextual guidance to assist users in navigating features.
Acceptance Criteria:
Users can access tips or tutorials within any page
Step-by-step guides appear when needed (e.g., posting a listing, sending a message)
Help content updates automatically as new features are added

19. Predictive Availability Alerts
Description:
The system should predict and notify students about upcoming apartment availability.
Acceptance Criteria:
System analyzes trends and past listings to forecast openings
Alerts are sent 1–2 weeks before expected availability
Users can opt in/out of predictive notifications

20. Eco-Friendly Data Usage
Description:
The system should optimize network usage to reduce data consumption for students on limited plans.
Acceptance Criteria:
Images and media are compressed without quality loss
Only essential content loads on low-bandwidth connections
Data usage per session is tracked and optimized


